IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch1-first-schedule.l4: the First Schedule (additional powers of the General Division).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 5462-5714).  Answers seams 1 and 2 of PLAN.md; the asking sections are ss 18(2) and 18I(1)(a), in scja1's range.
-- Each paragraph is a power of the court.  Read for the person it can be used against (the seat's litigant), "the court may do X in this case" is JUST TRUE where the paragraph's
-- conditions are met; JUST FALSE only where the paragraph's own wording says no ("where", "in any case in which", "excluding", "does not affect", "means");
-- NOTHING where the paragraph is only descriptive and the case falls outside the description, or where the court is not the General Division.
-- How a power is exercised ("in such manner as may be prescribed by Rules of Court") is left to the Rules of Court, which are not among the sources.

§ `First Schedule: additional powers of the General Division`

-- src:5462 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:5464 | Sections 18(2) and 18I(1)(a)
-- src:5466 | ADDITIONAL POWERS OF GENERAL DIVISION
@ref First Schedule (heading) (src:5462-5466)
-- One constructor per paragraph, plus a constructor for a power the Schedule does not set out.
DECLARE `sch 1 power` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 1 the power to issue a direction, order or writ, including a prerogative order`
    `sch 1 para 2 the power to partition land, direct a sale instead of partition, or order land sold`
    `sch 1 para 3 the power to order land charged or mortgaged instead of sold`
    `sch 1 para 4 the power to grant relief by way of interpleader and to order a sale`
    `sch 1 para 5 the power to preserve the subject matter, evidence and assets`
    `sch 1 para 6 the power to direct interest to be paid`
    `sch 1 para 7 the power to enlarge or abridge time`
    `sch 1 para 8 the power to enforce a judgment`
    `sch 1 para 9 the power to dismiss or stay proceedings`
    `sch 1 para 10 the power to transfer proceedings`
    `sch 1 para 11 the power to allow a defence of set-off`
    `sch 1 para 12 the power to order discovery`
    `sch 1 para 13 the power to award costs`
    `sch 1 para 14 the power to grant all reliefs and remedies at law and in equity`
    `sch 1 para 15 the power to order interim payments`
    `sch 1 para 16 the power to award provisional damages for personal injuries`
    `sch 1 para 17 the power to order damages for personal injuries to be paid in periodic instalments`
    `sch 1 para 18 the power to attach deposits with a financial institution`
    `sch 1 para 19 the power to order a medical examination of a party`
    `sch 1 para 20 the power to appoint an examiner of a child or person and to bar other evidence`
    `sch 1 para 21 the power to order mediation, counselling, intervention sessions or a family support programme`
    `sch 1 para 21A the power to conduct a mediation or to appoint a person to conduct it`
    `sch 1 para 22 the power to require a late filing charge`
    `sch 1 para 23 the power to order amicable resolution`
    `sch 1 another power that the First Schedule does not set out`

-- Seam 1 of PLAN.md.  s 18(2) says "Without limiting subsection (1)", so a power the Schedule does not set out may still be the General Division's under another written law:
-- the answer for it is NOTHING and never JUST FALSE.
GIVEN power IS A `sch 1 power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 the power is one set out in the First Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): s 18(1) gives the General Division the powers vested in it by any written law, and s 18(2) adds the First Schedule "without limiting" that
    WHEN `sch 1 another power that the First Schedule does not set out` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Seam 2 of PLAN.md.  Para 1 reaches "any direction, order or writ ... for any other purpose", so a power the Schedule does not set out may also be the paragraph 1 power: NOTHING.
GIVEN power IS A `sch 1 power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1 the power is the power under paragraph 1` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `sch 1 para 1 the power to issue a direction, order or writ, including a prerogative order` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): para 1 reaches a direction, order or writ "for any other purpose", and the Schedule does not set out this power
    WHEN `sch 1 another power that the First Schedule does not set out` THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the power is set out under another numbered paragraph of the Schedule, not paragraph 1
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- Scope: "Additional powers of General Division".  The Singapore International Commercial Court has its share of these powers through s 18I(1), which is another part's section.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 the power is the General Division's` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `General Division`
    THEN answer
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule is headed "Additional powers of General Division", and what the Singapore International Commercial Court or the Family Division of the High Court may exercise is a question for s 18I(1) and for the Family Justice Act, outside the Schedule
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Helper: whether a list of conditions all hold.
GIVEN conditions IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 all of the conditions hold` MEANS
    NOT (elem FALSE conditions)

-- src:5468 | Prerogative orders
-- src:5470 | 1. Power to issue to any person or authority any direction, order or writ for the
-- src:5471 | enforcement of any right conferred by any written law or for any other purpose,
-- src:5472 | including the following prerogative orders:
-- src:5474 | (a) a Mandatory Order (formerly known as mandamus);
-- src:5476 | (b) a Prohibiting Order (formerly known as a prohibition);
-- src:5478 | (c) a Quashing Order (formerly known as certiorari); and
-- src:5480 | (d) an Order for Review of Detention (formerly known as a writ of habeas
-- src:5481 | corpus).
@ref First Schedule para 1 (src:5468-5481)
DECLARE `sch 1 para 1 the order or writ` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 1(a) a Mandatory Order`
    `sch 1 para 1(b) a Prohibiting Order`
    `sch 1 para 1(c) a Quashing Order`
    `sch 1 para 1(d) an Order for Review of Detention`
    `sch 1 para 1 another direction, order or writ`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      order IS A `sch 1 para 1 the order or writ`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1 the court may issue the direction, order or writ to a person or authority` MEANS
    -- the paragraph reaches "any direction, order or writ ... for the enforcement of any right conferred by any written law or for any other purpose, including" the four prerogative orders, so every constructor is within it
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court (JUST TRUE)

-- src:5483 | Partition and sale in lieu of partition
-- src:5485 | 2. Power to partition land and to direct a sale instead of partition in any action for
-- src:5486 | partition of land; and in any cause or matter relating to land, where it appears
-- src:5487 | necessary or expedient, to order the land or any part of it to be sold, and to give all
-- src:5488 | necessary and consequential directions.
@ref First Schedule para 2 (src:5483-5488)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the action is an action for partition of land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2 the court may partition land or direct a sale instead of partition` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the action is an action for partition of land`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the first limb is "in any action for partition of land" and says nothing of other actions
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:5483 | Partition and sale in lieu of partition
-- src:5485 | 2. Power to partition land and to direct a sale instead of partition in any action for
-- src:5486 | partition of land; and in any cause or matter relating to land, where it appears
-- src:5487 | necessary or expedient, to order the land or any part of it to be sold, and to give all
-- src:5488 | necessary and consequential directions.
@ref First Schedule para 2 (second limb) (src:5483-5488)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the cause or matter relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court necessary or expedient that the land or part of it be sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2 the court may order land sold in a cause or matter relating to land` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF NOT `the cause or matter relates to land`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the second limb speaks of "any cause or matter relating to land"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `it appears to the court necessary or expedient that the land or part of it be sold`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it appears necessary or expedient"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5490 | Charge or mortgage in lieu of sale of land
-- src:5492 | 3. Power to order land to be charged or mortgaged (as the case may be) in any
-- src:5493 | case in which there is jurisdiction to order a sale.
@ref First Schedule para 3 (src:5490-5493)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `there is jurisdiction in the case to order a sale of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3 the court may order land charged or mortgaged instead of sold` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `there is jurisdiction in the case to order a sale of the land`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any case in which there is jurisdiction to order a sale"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5495 | Interpleader
-- src:5497 | 4. Power to grant relief by way of interpleader —
-- src:5499 | (a) where the person seeking relief is under liability for any debt, money,
-- src:5500 | or goods or chattels, for or in respect of which the person has been or
-- src:5501 | expects to be, sued by 2 or more parties making adverse claims
-- src:5502 | thereon; and
@ref First Schedule para 4(a) (src:5495-5502)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the person seeking relief is under liability for a debt, money, or goods or chattels` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been, or expects to be, sued by 2 or more parties in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those parties make adverse claims on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4(a) the court may grant relief by way of interpleader to a person under liability to adverse claimants` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `sch 1 all of the conditions hold` (LIST
                  `the person seeking relief is under liability for a debt, money, or goods or chattels`
                , `the person has been, or expects to be, sued by 2 or more parties in respect of it`
                , `those parties make adverse claims on it`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person seeking relief is under liability ... and ... has been or expects to be sued by 2 or more parties making adverse claims"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5504 | (b) where a Sheriff, bailiff or other officer of court is charged with the
-- src:5505 | execution of process of court, and claim is made to any money or
-- src:5506 | goods or chattels taken or intended to be taken under or pursuant to an
-- src:5507 | enforcement order under any process, or to the proceeds or value of
-- src:5516 | any such goods or chattels by any person other than the person against
-- src:5517 | whom the process is issued,
@ref First Schedule para 4(b) (src:5504-5517)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `an officer of court is charged with the execution of process of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `claim is made to money, goods or chattels taken or intended to be taken under an enforcement order, or to their proceeds or value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made by a person other than the person against whom the process is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4(b) the court may grant relief by way of interpleader to an officer of court charged with execution` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `sch 1 all of the conditions hold` (LIST
                  `an officer of court is charged with the execution of process of court`
                , `claim is made to money, goods or chattels taken or intended to be taken under an enforcement order, or to their proceeds or value`
                , `the claim is made by a person other than the person against whom the process is issued`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Sheriff, bailiff or other officer of court is charged with the execution of process of court, and claim is made ... by any person other than the person against whom the process is issued"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5519 | and to order the sale of any property subject to interpleader proceedings.
@ref First Schedule para 4 (sale) (src:5519)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the property is subject to interpleader proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4 the court may order the sale of property subject to interpleader proceedings` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the property is subject to interpleader proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to order the sale of any property subject to interpleader proceedings" and says nothing of other property
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:5523 | Preservation of subject matter, evidence and assets to satisfy judgment
-- src:5525 | 5. Power before or after any proceedings are commenced to provide for —
-- src:5527 | (a) the interim preservation of property which is the subject matter of the
-- src:5528 | proceedings by sale or by injunction or the appointment of receiver or
-- src:5529 | the registration of a caveat or a lis pendens or in any manner
-- src:5530 | whatsoever;
-- src:5532 | (b) the preservation of evidence by seizure, detention, inspection,
-- src:5533 | photographing, the taking of samples, the conduct of experiments or
-- src:5534 | in any manner; and
-- src:5536 | (c) the preservation of assets for the satisfaction of any judgment which
-- src:5537 | has been or may be made.
@ref First Schedule para 5 (src:5523-5537)
DECLARE `sch 1 para 5 the purpose of the order` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 5(a) the interim preservation of property which is the subject matter of the proceedings`
    `sch 1 para 5(b) the preservation of evidence`
    `sch 1 para 5(c) the preservation of assets for the satisfaction of a judgment which has been or may be made`
    `sch 1 para 5 another purpose`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      purpose IS A `sch 1 para 5 the purpose of the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 5 the court may provide for the preservation, before or after proceedings are commenced` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `sch 1 para 5(a) the interim preservation of property which is the subject matter of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 1 para 5(b) the preservation of evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 1 para 5(c) the preservation of assets for the satisfaction of a judgment which has been or may be made` THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names three purposes and does not say it is limited to them
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)

-- src:5539 | Interest
-- src:5541 | 6. Power to direct interest to be paid on damages, or debts (whether the debts are
-- src:5542 | paid before or after commencement of proceedings) or judgment debts, or on sums
-- src:5543 | found due on taking accounts between parties, or on sums found due and unpaid
-- src:5544 | by receivers or other persons liable to account to the court.
@ref First Schedule para 6 (src:5539-5544)
DECLARE `sch 1 para 6 the sum` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 6 damages`
    `sch 1 para 6 debts, whether paid before or after commencement of proceedings`
    `sch 1 para 6 judgment debts`
    `sch 1 para 6 sums found due on taking accounts between parties`
    `sch 1 para 6 sums found due and unpaid by receivers or other persons liable to account to the court`
    `sch 1 para 6 another sum`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      sum IS A `sch 1 para 6 the sum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6 the court may direct interest to be paid on the sum` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (CONSIDER sum
         WHEN `sch 1 para 6 another sum` THEN
             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names five kinds of sum and does not say it is limited to them
             NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)

-- src:5546 | Time
-- src:5548 | 7. Power to enlarge or abridge the time prescribed by any written law for doing
-- src:5549 | any act or taking any proceeding, whether the application therefor is made before
-- src:5550 | or after the expiration of the time prescribed, but this provision does not affect any
-- src:5551 | written law relating to limitation.
@ref First Schedule para 7 (src:5546-5551)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the time was prescribed by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that written law is a written law relating to limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7 the court may enlarge or abridge the time` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF NOT `the time was prescribed by a written law`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the time prescribed by any written law", and the paragraph says nothing of a time fixed in another way
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `that written law is a written law relating to limitation`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this provision does not affect any written law relating to limitation"
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:5553 | Enforcement of judgment
-- src:5555 | 8. Power to enforce a judgment of the court in any manner which may be
-- src:5556 | prescribed by any written law or by Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules.
@ref First Schedule para 8 (src:5553-5556)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 8 the court may enforce its judgment in a manner prescribed by a written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules` MEANS
    -- the manner is for the written law or the Rules, which are not among the sources
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court (JUST TRUE)

-- src:5558 | Stay of proceedings
-- src:5560 | 9. Power to dismiss or stay proceedings where the matter in question is res
-- src:5561 | judicata between the parties, or where by reason of multiplicity of proceedings in
-- src:5562 | any court or courts or by reason of a court in Singapore not being the appropriate
-- src:5563 | forum the proceedings ought not to be continued.
@ref First Schedule para 9 (src:5558-5563)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the matter in question is res judicata between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of multiplicity of proceedings in any court or courts the proceedings ought not to be continued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of a court in Singapore not being the appropriate forum the proceedings ought not to be continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 9 the court may dismiss or stay the proceedings` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the matter in question is res judicata between the parties`
            OR `by reason of multiplicity of proceedings in any court or courts the proceedings ought not to be continued`
            OR `by reason of a court in Singapore not being the appropriate forum the proceedings ought not to be continued`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the matter in question is res judicata between the parties, or where ... the proceedings ought not to be continued"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

