              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5634 | Examination and assessment of child, etc.
-- src:5636 | 20. Power, in any proceedings involving the custody or welfare of a child or
-- src:5637 | involving a person —
-- src:5639 | (a) to appoint a registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor,
-- src:5640 | social worker or mental health professional to examine and assess the
-- src:5641 | child or person (as the case may be) for the purposes of preparing
-- src:5642 | expert evidence for use in those proceedings; and
-- src:5644 | (b) to prohibit from being adduced in those proceedings any evidence
-- src:5645 | arising out of an examination or assessment of the child or person by
-- src:5646 | any person who is not so appointed.
@ref First Schedule para 20(a) (src:5634-5646)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the proceedings involve the custody or welfare of a child, or involve a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be appointed is a registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to prepare expert evidence for use in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 20(a) the court may appoint a professional to examine and assess the child or person` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `sch 1 all of the conditions hold` (LIST
                  `the proceedings involve the custody or welfare of a child, or involve a person`
                , `the person to be appointed is a registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health professional`
                , `the purpose is to prepare expert evidence for use in those proceedings`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "in any proceedings involving the custody or welfare of a child or involving a person", to appoint one of the five kinds of professional, for the purpose of expert evidence
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:5634 | Examination and assessment of child, etc.
-- src:5636 | 20. Power, in any proceedings involving the custody or welfare of a child or
-- src:5637 | involving a person —
-- src:5639 | (a) to appoint a registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor,
-- src:5640 | social worker or mental health professional to examine and assess the
-- src:5641 | child or person (as the case may be) for the purposes of preparing
-- src:5642 | expert evidence for use in those proceedings; and
-- src:5644 | (b) to prohibit from being adduced in those proceedings any evidence
-- src:5645 | arising out of an examination or assessment of the child or person by
-- src:5646 | any person who is not so appointed.
@ref First Schedule para 20(b) (src:5634-5646)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the proceedings involve the custody or welfare of a child, or involve a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence arises out of an examination or assessment by a person who was not appointed under paragraph 20(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 20(b) the court may prohibit the evidence from being adduced` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the proceedings involve the custody or welfare of a child, or involve a person`
            AND `the evidence arises out of an examination or assessment by a person who was not appointed under paragraph 20(a)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any evidence arising out of an examination or assessment of the child or person by any person who is not so appointed"
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:5648 | Ordering mediation, counselling, attendance at professional clinical or
-- src:5649 | therapeutic intervention sessions or participation in family support
-- src:5650 | programme or activity
-- src:5652 | 21.—(1) Power to order any party to any proceedings, or any child involved in
-- src:5653 | or whose custody or welfare is involved in the proceedings —
-- src:5655 | (a) to undergo any mediation or other alternative dispute resolution
-- src:5656 | process or counselling, or to participate in any family support
-- src:5657 | programme or activity, directed by the court; and
-- src:5659 | (b) to attend any professional clinical or therapeutic intervention sessions
-- src:5660 | directed by the court.
@ref First Schedule para 21(1) (src:5648-5660)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the person is a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child involved in, or whose custody or welfare is involved in, the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 21(1) the court may order the person to undergo mediation, counselling or a family support programme, or to attend intervention sessions` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the person is a party to the proceedings` OR `the person is a child involved in, or whose custody or welfare is involved in, the proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any party to any proceedings, or any child involved in or whose custody or welfare is involved in the proceedings"
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:5662 | (2) In this paragraph, “family support programme or activity” means any
-- src:5663 | programme or activity carried out for the purpose of addressing or resolving any
-- src:5664 | relationship issue or relationship problem between spouses or former spouses,
-- src:5665 | between siblings or between parent and child.
@ref First Schedule para 21(2) (src:5662-5665)
DECLARE `sch 1 para 21(2) the relationship` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 21(2) between spouses or former spouses`
    `sch 1 para 21(2) between siblings`
    `sch 1 para 21(2) between parent and child`
    `sch 1 para 21(2) another relationship`

GIVEN `the programme or activity is carried out for the purpose of addressing or resolving a relationship issue or relationship problem` IS A BOOLEAN
      relationship IS A `sch 1 para 21(2) the relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 21(2) the programme or activity is a family support programme or activity` MEANS
    IF `the programme or activity is carried out for the purpose of addressing or resolving a relationship issue or relationship problem`
       AND NOT (relationship EQUALS `sch 1 para 21(2) another relationship`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'family support programme or activity' means any programme or activity carried out for the purpose of addressing or resolving any relationship issue or relationship problem between spouses or former spouses, between siblings or between parent and child"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5676 | Power to appoint mediators
-- src:5678 | 21A. Where a court orders any party to any proceedings, or any child involved in
-- src:5679 | or whose custody or welfare is involved in the proceedings, to undergo any
-- src:5680 | mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process, the court also has the
-- src:5681 | following powers:
-- src:5683 | (a) to conduct the mediation or other alternative dispute resolution
-- src:5684 | process;
-- src:5686 | (b) to appoint a Judge, a Registrar, an officer of the Supreme Court, or any
-- src:5687 | other person, to conduct the mediation or other alternative dispute
-- src:5688 | resolution process.
@ref First Schedule para 21A (src:5676-5688)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court has ordered a party, or a child involved in the proceedings, to undergo mediation or another alternative dispute resolution process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 21A the court may conduct the process, or appoint a Judge, a Registrar, an officer of the Supreme Court or any other person to conduct it` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the court has ordered a party, or a child involved in the proceedings, to undergo mediation or another alternative dispute resolution process`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court orders any party to any proceedings, or any child ..., to undergo any mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process, the court also has the following powers"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5692 | Late filing charge
-- src:5694 | 22. Power, in any case where a person fails to file any document within the
-- src:5695 | period (for the filing of that document) specified in any order or direction of a
-- src:5696 | court, any Rules of Court or any practice directions issued by the Registrar, to
-- src:5697 | require the person to pay a late filing charge, of such amount as may be prescribed
-- src:5698 | in the Rules of Court, for each day, after the expiry of that period, that that
-- src:5699 | document remains unfiled.
@ref First Schedule para 22 (the power) (src:5692-5699)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the document was required to be filed within a period specified in an order or direction of a court, in Rules of Court or in practice directions issued by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE
      `the date the document was filed, or the date the charge is worked out to if it is still unfiled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 22 the court may require the person to pay a late filing charge` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court
        (IF `the document was required to be filed within a period specified in an order or direction of a court, in Rules of Court or in practice directions issued by the Registrar`
            AND `the date the document was filed, or the date the charge is worked out to if it is still unfiled` > `the last day of that period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any case where a person fails to file any document within the period (for the filing of that document) specified"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:5692 | Late filing charge
-- src:5694 | 22. Power, in any case where a person fails to file any document within the
-- src:5695 | period (for the filing of that document) specified in any order or direction of a
-- src:5696 | court, any Rules of Court or any practice directions issued by the Registrar, to
-- src:5697 | require the person to pay a late filing charge, of such amount as may be prescribed
-- src:5698 | in the Rules of Court, for each day, after the expiry of that period, that that
-- src:5699 | document remains unfiled.
@ref First Schedule para 22 (the charge) (src:5692-5699)
-- The charge is "for each day, after the expiry of that period, that that document remains unfiled".
-- Fork: the day the document is filed is not counted (the document did not "remain unfiled" for the whole of that day).  A document filed on the day after the last day of the period therefore draws no daily charge.
-- The amount is "such amount as may be prescribed in the Rules of Court", which is not among the sources: it is an input.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the document was required to be filed within a period specified in an order or direction of a court, in Rules of Court or in practice directions issued by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE
      `the date the document was filed, or the date the charge is worked out to if it is still unfiled` IS A DATE
      `the daily late filing charge prescribed in the Rules of Court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 22 the late filing charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1 para 22 the court may require the person to pay a late filing charge` court `the document was required to be filed within a period specified in an order or direction of a court, in Rules of Court or in practice directions issued by the Registrar` `the last day of that period` `the date the document was filed, or the date the charge is worked out to if it is still unfiled`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (`the daily late filing charge prescribed in the Rules of Court`
              * (`the date the document was filed, or the date the charge is worked out to if it is still unfiled` - `the last day of that period` - 1))
    -- the paragraph gives no power to require a charge where the document was filed in time, so none is payable under it
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule is headed "Additional powers of General Division"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5701 | Ordering parties to attempt to resolve dispute by amicable resolution
-- src:5703 | 23.—(1) Power to order any party to any proceedings to attempt to resolve any
-- src:5704 | dispute by amicable resolution.
@ref First Schedule para 23(1) (src:5701-5704)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 23(1) the court may order a party to attempt to resolve a dispute by amicable resolution` MEANS
    `sch 1 the power is the General Division's` court (JUST TRUE)

-- src:5706 | (2) In this paragraph, “amicable resolution” means —
-- src:5708 | (a) settlement of an action or appeal relating to a dispute; or
-- src:5710 | (b) resolution of a dispute other than by litigation, whether in whole or in
-- src:5711 | part.
@ref First Schedule para 23(2) (src:5706-5711)
DECLARE `sch 1 para 23(2) the thing` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 23(2)(a) settlement of an action or appeal relating to a dispute`
    `sch 1 para 23(2)(b) resolution of a dispute other than by litigation, whether in whole or in part`
    `sch 1 para 23(2) another thing`

GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1 para 23(2) the thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 23(2) the thing is amicable resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `sch 1 para 23(2) another thing` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'amicable resolution' means (a) settlement of an action or appeal relating to a dispute; or (b) resolution of a dispute other than by litigation, whether in whole or in part"
        JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
